WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.103
A Text Field stores text, but it can appear as a plain box,

00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:08.954
an email box, a color input, or a set of radio buttons.

00:00:08.954 --> 00:00:11.731
Editors decide how a value is entered.

00:00:11.731 --> 00:00:15.140
Display modes decide how it appears on the site.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.457
A content field stores one kind of value.

00:00:22.457 --> 00:00:26.502
A Text Field stores text, a Numeric Field stores a number, and a

00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:28.294
Date Field stores a date.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:32.340
Whatever the field looks like, it stores the same kind of value.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.242
The editor is what you see on the edit screen of a content item.

00:00:37.242 --> 00:00:41.157
A Numeric Field can be a number box, a slider, or a spinner.

00:00:41.157 --> 00:00:45.190
The editor changes how a value is entered, not what is stored.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.921
The display mode is what visitors see on the site.

00:00:48.921 --> 00:00:52.275
A Text Field can show its text as it is, or as a heading.

00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:56.480
You choose the editor and the display mode in the settings of each field.

00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:05.434
Design, Content Definition, Content Types lists the content types of the site.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:09.549
Typing Workshop in the Search box narrows the list to that type, and

00:01:09.549 --> 00:01:11.273
its Edit button opens it.

00:01:11.735 --> 00:01:15.975
The Fields list shows the three fields of Workshop, each with its kind

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.258
next to its name.

00:01:17.258 --> 00:01:18.987
Seats is a Numeric Field.

00:01:18.987 --> 00:01:22.055
Its Edit button opens the settings of that field.

00:01:22.512 --> 00:01:27.556
The settings of Seats include a Minimum and a Maximum, here zero and forty.

00:01:27.556 --> 00:01:31.852
Editors such as Slider use them as the two ends of their range.

00:01:32.318 --> 00:01:37.737
Below the settings, a drop-down list answers the question What type of editor should be used?

00:01:37.737 --> 00:01:39.105
Number is selected.

00:01:39.105 --> 00:01:40.528
Let's choose Slider.

00:01:41.021 --> 00:01:43.342
Save returns to the content type.

00:01:43.342 --> 00:01:47.568
Next to Seats, a badge with the name of the editor, Slider, shows

00:01:47.568 --> 00:01:49.591
which editor the field uses.

00:01:50.058 --> 00:01:52.370
Let's open the New Workshop page.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:57.113
Seats shows a slider track under its number box, running from the minimum,

00:01:57.113 --> 00:01:59.128
zero, to the maximum, forty.

00:01:59.591 --> 00:02:03.840
Dragging the handle changes the number in the box, and typing a number

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.740
in the box moves the handle.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.591
Both set the same value, the number of seats.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.119
Some editors bring settings of their own.

00:02:15.119 --> 00:02:18.281
Skill Level is a Text Field that should hold one of a few

00:02:18.281 --> 00:02:20.340
levels, so let's open its settings.

00:02:20.803 --> 00:02:26.193
Choosing Predefined List in the editor drop-down list reveals the settings of that editor.

00:02:26.193 --> 00:02:29.281
One asks What type of list editor should be used?

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:32.987
Below it, a table holds an Option Label and a Value for each

00:02:32.987 --> 00:02:35.513
option, here Beginner and Intermediate.

00:02:35.984 --> 00:02:39.762
The list editor can be a Drop down list or Radio buttons, and

00:02:39.762 --> 00:02:41.511
let's pick Radio buttons.

00:02:41.511 --> 00:02:45.571
Add an option adds a row, and typing the label, Advanced, fills in

00:02:45.571 --> 00:02:46.924
the value as well.

00:02:47.377 --> 00:02:51.130
Each option also has a radio button, under the title Default?

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:54.268
Selecting one makes that option the default value.

00:02:54.268 --> 00:02:56.397
Let's leave them all unselected.

00:02:56.873 --> 00:03:01.743
Save stores the options with the field, and the page returns to the content type.

00:03:02.205 --> 00:03:06.410
On the New Workshop page, Skill Level is a set of radio buttons,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.972
one for each option.

00:03:07.972 --> 00:03:10.315
Choosing Intermediate selects it.

00:03:14.184 --> 00:03:16.659
Display modes follow the same pattern.

00:03:16.659 --> 00:03:20.991
Headline is a Text Field, and its Edit button opens the settings, where

00:03:20.991 --> 00:03:23.804
the display mode is chosen below the editor.

00:03:24.259 --> 00:03:29.020
A drop-down list answers the question What type of display mode should be used?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.532
Standard is selected.

00:03:30.532 --> 00:03:31.989
Let's choose Header.

00:03:32.442 --> 00:03:34.989
A setting appears for the display mode:

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:37.083
Select the header level to use.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:42.232
Let's choose H2 and Save, and the content type shows a Header badge next to Headline.

00:03:42.685 --> 00:03:48.941
On the site, the Headline of the Spring Pottery Evening workshop appears as a second-level heading.

00:03:48.941 --> 00:03:53.945
A display mode changes only what visitors see; the stored text stays the same.

00:03:58.145 --> 00:04:01.099
Each field offers its own editors.

00:04:01.099 --> 00:04:07.744
A Text Field offers Standard, Code Mirror, Color, Email, Icon picker, Monaco editor,

00:04:07.744 --> 00:04:11.362
Multi-line, Phone, Predefined List and Url.

00:04:11.362 --> 00:04:16.605
A Numeric Field offers Number, Range, Select, Slider and Spinner.

00:04:17.355 --> 00:04:22.362
A Boolean Field offers Standard and Switch, and a Multi Text Field offers

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.960
Standard, Checkbox List and Picker.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.066
A Date Field offers Standard and Localized.

00:04:28.066 --> 00:04:32.185
The Date Time Field and the Time Field offer Standard only.

00:04:32.935 --> 00:04:35.014
Display modes are less common.

00:04:35.014 --> 00:04:39.460
A Text Field offers Standard and Header, and a User Picker Field offers

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.192
Standard and User Names.

00:04:41.192 --> 00:04:45.465
Every other field of the Content Fields module offers Standard only.

00:04:47.465 --> 00:04:49.711
One field can serve many purposes:

00:04:49.711 --> 00:04:54.091
the editor shapes the edit screen, the display mode shapes the site, and

00:04:54.091 --> 00:04:56.225
the stored value stays the same.

00:04:56.225 --> 00:04:57.685
Thanks for watching.

